# plans/plan_dx9.md D9-A5 scene corpus: colored_linelist_quad
# The second never-before-exercised PrimitiveType in the corpus (after colored_trianglestrip_quad,
# which closed TriangleStrip): every scene before that one used TriangleList exclusively.
# PrimitiveType.LineList draws N/2 independent 2-vertex line segments -- genuinely different from
# LineStrip (a single connected polyline) and from every triangle-based topology already covered.
# No code changes needed: GraphicsDevice::PrimitiveVerts()/ToD3D9Topology() already handle
# LineList unconditionally, and the scene format has supported it since D9-A3's own original
# design.
#
# Two SEPARATE, non-touching horizontal line segments at clean, exactly-pixel-centered Y rows
# (avoids the half-pixel/AA boundary ambiguity D9-91 already taught this corpus to watch for --
# horizontal lines at integer-mapped Y coordinates have no diagonal antialiasing edge case). RED
# at y=0.5 (screen y=64), GREEN at y=-0.5 (screen y=192), same X range for both. Sampling the
# midpoint of each line proves each segment paints its own color; sampling the row exactly between
# them (screen y=128, background CornflowerBlue) proves LineList draws two INDEPENDENT segments,
# not a single connected 4-vertex polyline (which LineStrip would instead produce from the same
# vertex data) -- a broken vertex-count<->primitiveCount conversion for LineList (e.g. treating 4
# vertices as primitiveCount=4 instead of 2, or as a single continuous strip) would show up as
# missing color, a connecting line between the two rows, or a shifted/degenerate segment.
width=256
height=256
profile=HiDef
clearcolor=100,149,237,255
vertexcolor=true
lighting=false
primitive=LineList
vertex=-0.8,0.5,0,255,0,0,255
vertex=0.8,0.5,0,255,0,0,255
vertex=-0.8,-0.5,0,0,255,0,255
vertex=0.8,-0.5,0,0,255,0,255
